{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKPairSurjective","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKPairSurjective","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedWordOfPermSurj","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedShapeOfPositions","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedRSKSurjective"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_rskPair_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.exists_rskPair_eq","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKPairSurjective.lean#L101-L133","doc":"**`rskPair` is surjective onto standard pairs.** Every pair of standard Young tableaux of a\ncommon shape `μ` is the RSK image of a permutation of `Fin |μ|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rskPairWord_eq_of_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.rskPairWord_eq_of_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKPairSurjective.lean#L81-L99","doc":"**The RSK pair of a word that bridges to `(S_P, S_Q)` is `⟨μ, S_P, S_Q⟩`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shiftT_unshiftT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.shiftT_unshiftT","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKPairSurjective.lean#L73-L79","doc":"**`shiftT` undoes `unshiftT`** on a tableau of positive entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.map_pred_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.map_pred_succ","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKPairSurjective.lean#L62-L71","doc":"Shifting a row down and back up is the identity on positive entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sigma_pair_ext_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.sigma_pair_ext_entry","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKPairSurjective.lean#L51-L60","doc":"Extensionality for a diagram carrying a *pair* of tableaux. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.entry_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.entry_cast","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedRSKPairSurjective.lean#L46-L49","doc":"Transporting a standard tableau along an equality of diagrams does not move its entries. ","signatureChunk":0}]}